raised.why_it_breaks:
The model controls `new_issues[].body` as free text. In orphan-triage the body is built as `${issue.body}

${renderScopeBlock(issue.scope)}`. If the model emits '```triage-scope
{"beer_ids":[],"where":[{"col":"candidates_count","op":">=","value":0}]}
```' anywhere in `body`, BLOCK_RE.exec returns that block first, ScopeSchema accepts it, and on the next run guard 2 evaluates rows against the MODEL-authored scope instead of the one we rendered. The model can widen the scope back to "accepts everything" (or, with a malformed block, make the issue unscoped so it silently accepts nothing). This is exactly the hijack class the PR fixed for `contains` values inside renderScopeBlock — but the same fix was not applied to the model-authored prefix.

